4. React Fundamentals
Beginner level
This is the most important stage.
Topic	Explanation
Components	Reusable UI building blocks
JSX	Writing HTML-like syntax inside JavaScript
Functional Components	Components created using functions
Props	Passing data from parent to child
State	Managing changing component data
Events	Handling clicks, typing and form actions
Conditional Rendering	Displaying UI based on conditions
Lists	Displaying arrays using map()
Keys	Identifying list elements uniquely
Fragments	Grouping elements without extra DOM nodes
CSS Styling	Applying styles to components

Example 1: First React component
function App() {
    return (
        <div>
            <h1>Hello React!</h1>
            <p>Welcome to React Learning</p>
        </div>
    );
}

export default App;


Example 2: Props
function Student(props) {
    return <h2>Welcome {props.name}</h2>;
}

function App() {
    return (
        <div>
            <Student name="Venu" />
            <Student name="Rahul" />
        </div>
    );
}

export default App;


Output:
Welcome Venu
Welcome Rahul


Example 3: State using useState
import { useState } from "react";

function App() {
    const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

    return (
        <div>
            <h1>Count: {count}</h1>

            <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
                Increment
            </button>
        </div>
    );
}

export default App;


Understand how the UI updates when state changes.
5. React Hooks
Core React skills
Hooks allow functional components to use React features such as state, effects and context.
Hook	Purpose	Example use
useState	Store component state	Counter
useEffect	Synchronize with external systems	API calls
useContext	Share data across components	Authentication
useRef	Store references and mutable values	Input focus
useMemo	Cache calculated values	Expensive calculations
useCallback	Cache function definitions	Optimizing child components
useReducer	Manage complex state	Shopping cart
useId	Generate unique IDs	Form labels
Custom Hooks	Reuse stateful logic	useFetch

Example: useEffect
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

function App() {
    const [users, setUsers] = useState([]);

    useEffect(() => {
        fetch("https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users")
            .then(response => response.json())
            .then(data => setUsers(data));
    }, []);

    return (
        <div>
            <h1>Users</h1>

            {users.map(user => (
                <p key={user.id}>{user.name}</p>
            ))}
        </div>
    );
}

export default App;


Understand:
- What is an API?
- What is fetch()?
- What is useEffect()?
- What is a dependency array?
- What is cleanup?
- How to handle loading and error states?
